      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree, commenting to hopefully bring attention to this post.\n\nI'm sure there must've been some reason the 4 character minimum was introduced but I can't really understand why. There can only be so many 1-3 character names, why not just let early adopters claim them?\n\nAll this restriction does is make people get around it with odd characters and spaces between them which isn't ideal considering the name they're trying to mimic isn't taken, it's just not possible because of the character restriction.\n\nIf there is a valid reason, could someone on the team please clarify why this change was made if there are no plans to revert it?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-10-22T03:32:34.177Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In Asian countries, many people have shorter name than others. So 4 length limits is too small to express our names easily. Please let we can use much shorter name, at least CJK countries!",
